{
 "text": "Here is a Python function that calculates the n-th Fibonacci number iteratively:\n\n```python\ndef fib(n):\n    if n <= 0:\n        return \"Invalid input. The value must be positive.\"\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        a, b = 0, 1\n        for _ in range(n - 2):\n            a, b = b, a + b\n        return b\n\n# Example usage:\nprint(fib(10))  # Output: 55\n",
